From 4a64572d779fc5df2d819bd183523d6fbb7b0bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:42:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: give the 8 MiB pooled-sender ack wait a slow-host
 ceiling

test_pooled_sender_auto_flush_default_bytes_falls_back_to_8_mib sends one
8 MiB row and waits 5s for the ack. The QwpAckServer test fixture unmasks
each WebSocket frame byte by byte in pure Python, which on a riscv64 CI
runner takes longer than 5s for 8 MiB, so wait() times out with "no ack
progress" while the server is still reading the frame. Every other test in
the suite (858 of 859) passes.

wait() returns as soon as the ack arrives, so raising the ceiling costs
nothing on fast hosts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fixed 5s test timeout too short for the pure-Python mock server on slow riscv64 runners]
---
 test/test.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/test.py b/test/test.py
index 1ee125f..8418ab2 100755
--- a/test/test.py
+++ b/test/test.py
@@ -906,7 +906,7 @@ class TestQwpWebSocketApi(unittest.TestCase):
                         'events', columns={'value': 'x' * (8 * 1024 * 1024)},
                         at=qi.ServerTimestamp)
                     self.assertEqual(len(sender), 0)
-                    sender.wait(5000)
+                    sender.wait(120000)
 
             stats = server.snapshot()
 
